  "notes": "Drawn from one photo, N812VL (737-800, Sept 2026), left side, slightly from ahead. The belly under the purple sweep isn't seen; it's taken as purple aft of the sweep. Re-checked 2026-11-15 on N812VL against its windows and forward door (the photo is too far ahead of the aircraft for a reliable fit to the measured shape): the title starts about 0.9 m aft of the forward door's middle (x 0.155; it had been drawn over the door) and runs to x 0.378, baseline about 1.4 m under the window line (y -0.29), the l's top y 0.73, lowercase 0.78 of it; the fin title runs from 0.18 to 0.54 of the chord just above the root. The sweep's edge is a gentle curve, now smooth.",
